{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JoKZa6xvy3MsYXpptLUvCG","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87\",\"date\":\"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)\",\"refs\":\"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master\",\"body\":\"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException\\n\\nSince TRUNK-6799, AuthorizationAdvice and core's explicit privilege\\nchecks denied with Spring Security's AccessDeniedException rather than\\nAPIAuthenticationException. Code catching the old type stopped\\nrecognizing denials; webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST\\nanswered 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\\n\\nAPIAuthenticationException now extends AuthorizationDeniedException.\\nCore throws it again wherever it did before 3.0.0, and wherever a\\n@PreAuthorize or @PostAuthorize check names the missing privilege, so a\\ncatch on either type recognizes the denial. It stays deprecated in\\nfavour of AccessDeniedException, which every denial is.\\n\\nIt is no longer an APIException, so a module compiled against an earlier\\ncore whose bytecode treats it as one fails verification until rebuilt.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n* TRUNK-6823: Deny a failed isAuthenticated() with APIAuthenticationException too\\n\\n@PreAuthorize(\\\"isAuthenticated()\\\"), the migration guide's translation of a\\nno-value @Authorized, denied a logged-out caller with a plain\\nAuthorizationDeniedException where @Authorized throws\\nAPIAuthenticationException, so converting such a method changed what its\\ncallers catch. It now records the denial for\\nPrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager to report as AuthorizationAdvice does.\\n\\nTestInstallUtil throws APIAuthenticationException again, as before 3.0.0,\\nand the migration guide notes that the class is no longer an APIException.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"dkayiwa\",\"authorEmail\":\"dkayiwa@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Rafal Korytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3310bc1d9682151ac461faf0916ca3da7d5a88d0\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T14:06:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Follow-up: Re-add null privilege check and add guards\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1d0fb13892759020f6bc0824a097518d546024eb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T13:45:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6705: Reduce the overhead of the gzip filter (#6505)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1b5421a9a8d69030adb91124c3f9cb758dbc58a8\",\"date\":\"2026-07-24T11:14:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"TRUNK-6712: Cache flattened role privileges for privilege and superuser checks (#6383)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00\",\"message\":\"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"rkorytkowski\",\"authorEmail\":\"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055\",\"date\":\"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00\",\"message