},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/aop/AuthorizationAdviceTest.java\",\"additions\":35,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/api/APIAuthenticationExceptionTest.java\",\"additions\":70,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/api/context/DaemonTest.java\",\"additions\":16,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/api/context/UserContextTest.java\",\"additions\":15,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/notification/AlertServiceTest.java\",\"additions\":14,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/security/OpenmrsMethodSecurityConfigTest.java\",\"additions\":77,\"deletions\":2},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/security/OpenmrsPermissionEvaluatorTest.java\",\"additions\":22,\"deletions\":1},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/security/PreAuthorizeConversionEquivalenceTest.java\",\"additions\":14,\"deletions\":0},{\"path\":\"api/src/test/java/org/openmrs/util/ExceptionUtilTest.java\",\"additions\":3,\"deletions\":4},{\"path\":\"doc/AUTHORIZATION_MIGRATION.md\",\"additions\":16,\"deletions\":11},{\"path\":\"web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/TestInstallUtil.java\",\"additions\":2,\"deletions\":2},{\"path\":\"web/src/test/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/TestInstallUtilTest.java\",\"additions\":51,\"deletions\":0}],\"body\":\"## Description of what I changed\\n\\nSince TRUNK-6799, `AuthorizationAdvice` and core's explicit privilege checks deny with Spring Security's `AccessDeniedException` instead of `APIAuthenticationException`. Code that catches the old type no longer sees these denials. webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST now answers 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\\n\\nThis keeps `AccessDeniedException` as the type a denial is. It only makes the deprecated exception a subtype of it:\\n\\n- `APIAuthenticationException` now extends `AuthorizationDeniedException`. Its constructors keep their messages and causes, and it gains one that takes an `AuthorizationResult`. It stays `@Deprecated`, pointing new code at `AccessDeniedException`.\\n- `@Authorized` denies with it again (`AuthorizationAdvice`'s three throw sites), and so do the checks #6544 had switched to `AccessDeniedException`: `Daemon.runInNewDaemonThread`/`runNewDaemonTask`, `UserContext.becomeUser`, `AlertServiceImpl.getAlerts` and `TestInstallUtil.getResourceInputStream`.\\n- `PrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager` returns it as the result when a `@PreAuthorize`/`@PostAuthorize` check names the missing privilege, and when `isAuthenticated()` denies a caller who is not logged in. The second case carries \\\"Basic authentication required\\\", as `@Authorized()` does. Spring's default handler throws that result, so converting a method by the guide's translation table keeps what its callers catch. Only an expression that names neither, such as `denyAll()`, still denies with a plain `AuthorizationDeniedException`. URL rules are unchanged.\\n- `doc/AUTHORIZATION_MIGRATION.md`, `ExceptionUtil` and the exception's javadoc say so. The guide has a Pitfalls row for the `VerifyError` below.\\n\\nwebservices.rest still needs RESTWS-1056 (openmrs/openmrs-module-webservices.rest#767) for denials that are not an `APIAuthenticationException`.\\n\\n**Compatibility.** `APIAuthenticationException` is no longer an `APIException`.\\n\\n- **Compiled bytecode that treats it as one fails JVM verification.** A module built against an earlier core breaks until it is rebuilt.\\n- **Example: patientdocuments.** It has `catch (APIAuthenticationException | ContextAuthenticationException e)` in two controllers, which javac types as `APIException`. Its omod as built today, against core master, stops this branch's OpenMRS from starting: `VerifyError` while Spring maps `VisitSummaryPreviewController`. Rebuilt against this branch with no source change, it starts and works.\\n- **After this merges,** patientdocuments' 3.0 SNAPSHOT needs a rebuild before a server running it will start, as does any other module whose bytecode has that shape.\\n- **Scan of the RefApp 3.0 module builds:** 19 classes in the 29 module builds reference the exception. Only those two handlers have this bytecode shape, though other shapes are possible.\\n- **Source compatibility:** code that assigns it to an `APIException` stops compiling. `catch (APIException e)` no longer catches a denial core throws, which is already the case on master. After this change it also misses an `APIAuthenticationException` a module throws itself. 6 of the 29 RefApp 3.0 module builds throw one, and none of their catches relies on catching it as an `APIException`.\\n- **A catch naming both types stops compiling.** That covers `catch (AccessDeniedException | APIAuthenticationException e)`, and `catch (AccessDeniedException)` followed by `catch (APIAuthenticationException)`. Catch `AccessDeniedException` alone, which covers both before and after this change. openmrs/openmrs-module-legacyui#272 has four such catches, and openmrs/openmrs-module-legacyui#274 has two in `DWRAdministrationServiceTest`.\\n\\nVerified on core 3.0.0-SNAPSHOT with the RefApp 3.0 modules and the published webservices.rest 5.0.0-SNAPSHOT, using `GET /ws/rest/v1/patient?q=Anderson&v=default`:\\n\\n| Caller | build 435 (master) | this branch |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| No credentials | 500 `AuthorizationDeniedException` | 401 \\\"User is not logged in [Privileges required: Get Patients]\\\" |\\n| Wrong password | 500 | 401 |\\n| Logged in, without Get Patients | 500 | 403 \\\"User is logged in but doesn't have the relevant privilege [Privileges required: Get Patients]\\\" |\\n\\nOn the same server, the `@PreAuthorize(\\\"hasAuthority('Get Providers')\\\")` check in `ProviderService.getAllProviders`, reached through `GET /ws/rest/v1/account` by a user with Get Users but not Get Providers, answers 403 \\\"[Privileges required: Get Providers]\\\" (500 on build 435). The setup wizard's testing install still reports \\\"Invalid username or password\\\" when the remote server rejects the credentials. All 29 modules start, once patientdocuments is rebuilt as described above.\\n\\nlegacyui master's `DWRAdministrationServiceTest`, which catches `APIAuthenticationException`, has 2 errors against build 435 and passes against this branch.\\n\\nLeft as they are:\\n- Core's own `catch (APIException)` fallbacks still miss a denial, as they do on master. For example, `PersonName.getFullName` reads a global property that needs Get Global Properties. That is openmrs/openmrs-core#6669, fixed by openmrs/openmrs-core#6671.\\n- The deprecation note and the guide's Pitfalls row call `AccessDeniedException` what every denial is. `Context.requirePrivilege` still denies with `ContextAuthenticationException`, an `APIException`. `APIAuthenticationException` never covered that case either.\\n\\n## Issue I worked on\\n\\nsee https://issues.openmrs.org/browse/TRUNK-6823\\n\\n## Checklist: I completed these to help reviewers :)\\n\\n- [x] My IDE is configured to follow the [**code style**](https://wiki.openmrs.org/display/docs/Java+Conventions) of this project.\\n- [x] I have **added tests** to cover my changes.\\n- [x] I ran `./mvnw clean package` right before creating this pull request and added all formatting changes to my commit.\\n- [x] All new and existing **tests passed**: `mvn clean verify` from the root, with api at 5621 tests (45 skipped) and web at 310, none failing.\\n- [x] My pull request is **based on the latest changes** of the master branch.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\\n\",\"nextOffset\":null,\"truncated\":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2fddec62-6800-4d87-a7fa-903e577e1b61","uuid":"2fa99330-96f4-414d-a59c-57d1957cdfaf","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:06:45.455Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core\",\"number\":6674,\"kind\":\"pr\",\"title\":\"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthen